(7294047, 1136873, 37858, '<td valign="top">Beautiful image, Mark.  I knew this challenge would play to your strengths, although I didn''t recognize the location so I wasn''t sure this was yours.  Love everything about it.  Congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'Beautiful image, Mark.  I knew this challenge would play to your strengths, although I didn''t recognize the location so I wasn''t sure this was yours.  Love everything about it.  Congrats on the ribbon.', '2014-12-19 02:22:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7294056, 1136684, 42181, '<td valign="top"><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=156466" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">backdoorhippie</a> Thanks for you comment, i think a number of voters missed the fact that this was a 30 MINUTE exposure. For me it was more about the technique, i realise that it isn''t a great "looking" picture but that wasn''t really the aim.<br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=13077" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">MadMan2k</a> I hope you have taken the time to come back and read the details and that the shot now works for you.<br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=50695" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">posthumous</a> It is slightly more than just a backwards upside-down camera. Check out the details of the shot. I turned one of the rooms in my house into a camera and then took a picture of the result, this took 30 minutes. Thanks for the hanging, at least it''s in your fantasy gallery :-)</td>', ' backdoorhippie Thanks for you comment, i think a number of voters missed the fact that this was a 30 MINUTE exposure. For me it was more about the technique, i realise that it isn''t a great "looking" picture but that wasn''t really the aim. MadMan2k I hope you have taken the time to come back and read the details and that the shot now works for you. posthumous It is slightly more than just a backwards upside-down camera. Check out the details of the shot. I turned one of the rooms in my house into a camera and then took a picture of the result, this took 30 minutes. Thanks for the hanging, at least it''s in your fantasy gallery :-)', '2014-12-19 04:04:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(7294059, 1136996, 118154, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, still enjoying this image.</td>', 'Congratulations, still enjoying this image.', '2014-12-19 04:11:51.000000', NULL, 0);
